{"name": "implement-catalog", "agent_type": "general-purpose", "description": "Implement course catalog app", "mode": "background", "prompt": "
You are implementing a university course catalog Blazor Web App. The project is already scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog` using Static SSR (`dotnet new blazor -int None`).

## Requirements
- Browse departments and courses in a searchable, filterable list
- View course detail pages (description, schedule, credits, instructor bio)
- Students submit an enrollment request form (name, student ID, course selection) — standard HTML form POST, no wizards or real-time validation
- Homepage shows featured courses and department links
- No authentication
- Hosted on university intranet with fast connectivity

## Architecture Decisions
- Static SSR only (no @rendermode directives, no @onclick handlers)
- Forms use HTML POST with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` and `<AntiforgeryToken />`
- Navigation uses links and query strings with `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]`
- In-memory data service (no database needed for demo)

## Tasks

### 1. Create Data Models
Create `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Models/Department.cs`:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Department
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";
    public string Code { get; set; } = "";
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
}
```

Create `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Models/Course.cs`:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Course
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } = "";
    public string Code { get; set; } = "";
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
    public int Credits { get; set; }
    public string Schedule { get; set; } = "";
    public string InstructorName { get; set; } = "";
    public string InstructorBio { get; set; } = "";
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
    public string DepartmentName { get; set; } = "";
    public bool IsFeatured { get; set; }
}
```

Create `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Models/EnrollmentRequest.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class EnrollmentRequest
{
    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Name is required.")]
    public string StudentName { get; set; } = "";

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student ID is required.")]
    public string StudentId { get; set; } = "";

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    [Range(1, int.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    public int CourseId { get; set; }
}
```

### 2. Create Data Service
Create `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Services/ICatalogService.cs`:
```csharp
using UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Services;

public interface ICatalogService
{
    List<Department> GetDepartments();
    Department? GetDepartment(int id);
    List<Course> GetCourses(string? search = null, int? departmentId = null);
    Course? GetCourse(int id);
    List<Course> GetFeaturedCourses();
    void SubmitEnrollmentRequest(EnrollmentRequest request);
}
```

Create `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Services/CatalogService.cs` with an in-memory implementation that has realistic sample data:
- At least 4 departments (Computer Science, Mathematics, Physics, English)
- At least 3 courses per department with realistic titles, descriptions, schedules (e.g., "MWF 9:00-9:50 AM"), credits (3-4), instructor names and short bios
- Mark 3-4 courses as featured
- The SubmitEnrollmentRequest method just stores requests in a list (demo purposes)

### 3. Register the Service
Update `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Program.cs` to register `ICatalogService` as a singleton:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<ICatalogService, CatalogService>();
```
Add the appropriate using statement.

### 4. Update NavMenu
Edit `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Components/Layout/NavMenu.razor` to replace the Weather link with:
- Home
- Courses (href="courses")
- Enroll (href="enroll")

Update the navbar brand to "Course Catalog".

### 5. Delete Weather.razor
Delete `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Components/Pages/Weather.razor`

### 6. Create Homepage
Replace the content of `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Components/Pages/Home.razor` with a page that:
- Has a welcome heading and brief description
- Shows a "Featured Courses" section with cards (title, department, credits) linking to detail pages
- Shows a "Departments" section with links that navigate to the courses page filtered by department

Use `@inject ICatalogService CatalogService` to get data. Use Bootstrap classes for styling.

### 7. Create Courses List Page
Create `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Components/Pages/Courses.razor` at `@page "/courses"`:
- A search form (GET form with `method="get"`) that submits a search term and department filter
- Use `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]` for `Search` and `DepartmentId` parameters
- Show results in a table or card list with course code, title, department, credits
- Each course links to its detail page
- Department filter is a dropdown populated from the service

### 8. Create Course Detail Page
Create `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Components/Pages/CourseDetail.razor` at `@page "/courses/{Id:int}"`:
- Display course title, code, description, schedule, credits
- Show instructor name and bio
- Link back to courses list
- Link to enroll page with course pre-selected (href="enroll?courseId={Id}")

### 9. Create Enrollment Form Page
Create `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Components/Pages/Enroll.razor` at `@page "/enroll"`:
- Use `<EditForm>` with `Model` binding and `FormName="enrollment"` and `method="post"`
- Include `<AntiforgeryToken />`
- Fields: Student Name (text input), Student ID (text input), Course (select dropdown populated from service)
- Use `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` for the model
- Use `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]` for an optional `CourseId` parameter to pre-select a course
- Use `<DataAnnotationsValidator />` and `<ValidationSummary />`
- On successful submission, show a confirmation message
- Standard HTML form behavior, no wizards

### 10. Update _Imports.razor
Add to `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Components/_Imports.razor`:
```
@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Models
@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Services
```

### 11. Update MainLayout
Edit `/tmp/sv-7835cecf98ac40f6a7ec0a9d6a8f8b24/UniversityCourseCatalog/Components/Layout/MainLayout.razor` to change the top-row "About" link to "University Course Catalog" text or a relevant link.

### 12. Build and verify
Run `dotnet build` in the project directory to ensure everything compiles.

## Important Rules
- Do NOT use `@rendermode` anywhere
- Do NOT use `@onclick` or any event handlers
- Forms use HTML POST with EditForm + [SupplyParameterFromForm]
- Search/filter uses GET forms or query string links with [SupplyParameterFromQuery]
- Use Bootstrap classes for layout (already included in the template)
"}

